  data:  # 1e60
    kind: work_item  # 1e60
    title: "C# interface inheritance (interface IChild : IBase) emits no edge: interface symbols carry no base_classes"  # 1e60
    status: todo_hard  # 1e60
    priority: 2  # 1e60
    parent:  # 1e60
    tags:  # 1e60
    - analysis_quality  # 1e60
    isbefore: []  # 1e60
    duplicate_of: []  # 1e60
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1e60
    pr_ref:  # 1e60
    description: "Surfaced by WI-kalug-takiz-lumim-falaj-kopuf-tapor-kizof-sajur's family sweep (2026-09-30, branch jgstern-agent/fix/kalug-ts-interface-extends).\n\nC# interface inheritance emits NO edge: `interface IChild : IBase { void N(); }` gives IChild meta with no base_classes, so neither the analyzer nor the core inheritance linker sees the relation. The class case works (`class Impl : IChild` -> base_classes ['IChild'] -> Impl -implements-> IChild from the inheritance-linker).\n\nCode (relocate by name): csharp.py `_extract_base_list` (def ~645) is called from the class/struct branch (~745); the `interface_declaration` branch (~783) does not call it.\n\nREPRO: fixture c.cs = `interface IBase { void M(); }` / `interface IChild : IBase { void N(); }` / `class Impl : IChild { ... }`; `hypergumbo survey . --out f.json` -> only edge is Impl -implements-> IChild; IChild node meta = {'visibility_signal': 'default'}.\n\nExpected after a fix: IChild -extends-> IBase. With WI-kalug's core change (an interface/trait/protocol source's edges are `extends`), adding base_classes to C# interface symbols is enough; no edge-type work in csharp.py.\n\nNote: linkers/type_hierarchy.py `_extends_admits_dispatch` docstring states \"C# interface inheritance ... produce[s] extends edges between interface symbols\" -- not true on this repro."  # 1e60
    fields: {}  # 1e60
- op: discuss  # b1d3
  at: '2026-10-01T15:34:07Z'  # b1d3
  by: agent  # b1d3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b1d3
  clock: 2  # b1d3
  nonce: b1d3  # b1d3
  message: "From WI-nizug-lavig-duhob-finog-mudus-rizut-zidub-jurit (local branch `jgstern-agent/fix/nizug`, commit 8e1e058645, not merged): the `type_hierarchy._extends_admits_dispatch` docstring that claimed Go interface embedding and C# interface inheritance already produce `extends` edges between interface symbols is rewritten there. It now says no deny-list analyzer emits such a hop on the measured fixtures (C# `interface IB : IA`, Go `type RW interface { Reader; ... }`, Rust `trait Solid: Shape` all emit no edge, dev 4dfb1d645a) and names this item. Bearing on this item: once the producer emits the edge, the gate needs no change. With WI-kalug's core linker the edge is labelled `extends` (interface source), and the gate admits it because the child is abstract. Without WI-kalug the edge is `implements`, which the gate never touches. I ran WI-nizug's fixture with WI-kalug's core diff applied: the dispatches_to set was identical, and the only edge that changed was Java `IChild -> IBase` going from implements to extends."  # b1d3
