- op: discuss  # 3fda
  at: '2026-10-18T03:14:54Z'  # 3fda
  by: agent  # 3fda
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3fda
  clock: 4  # 3fda
  nonce: 3fda  # 3fda
  message: "Done in PR #1707 (dev 0d9ebbe80d). csharp.py's interface_declaration branch calls _extract_base_list like the class and struct branches, so an interface's bases land in meta[\"base_classes\"] and the inheritance linker emits extends (WI-kalug's rule). Behavioral evidence: test_csharp.py::TestCSharpInterfaceInheritance (red: IChild.meta None; green: {'base_classes': ['IBase', 'IDisposable']}); end to end, hypergumbo survey on the item's fixture now emits extends IChild -> IBase, implements Impl -> IChild, and dispatches_to IBase.M -> Impl.M (type-hierarchy linker), where before only the implements edge existed. The type_hierarchy docstring that claimed this hop emitted no edge is corrected."  # 3fda
